00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:37.091
<v Mike Hall>Hi, I'm Mike, sitting down again with Ryan Briones and Ethan Gunderson. These guys created Gathers Us. It's a website for managing user group events and also the founders of the Chicago DB user group. Thanks, Ryan and Ethan, for sitting down again. We had a little technical snafu beforehand. So what we discussed earlier is that Gathers Us had a pretty interesting origin, that it was based off of a need that you had in creating Chicago DB. Can you describe a little bit about some of the inception of Gathers Us and what that is in?

00:00:37.091 --> 00:00:49.432
<v Ethan Gunderson, Ryan Briones>I mean, it's used for several user groups. I've used it myself, and I know GeekFest uses it. It's a great success, and you get a lot of sign-ups, I mean, well over 100 each week.

00:00:49.432 --> 00:00:52.344
<v Mike Hall>How did Gathers Us come out of Chicago DB?

00:00:52.344 --> 00:01:58.692
<v Ethan Gunderson, Ryan Briones>Well, there were two major things that happened. And one, we were too cheap to use a tool that costs money. There's a couple of them out there, a big one. Which was kind of the biggest impetus for us to create our own, especially when we kind of like had this idea for the group, but we didn't know how it was going to, you know, if it was going to be successful or not. Pay money for something that was just going to be, that wasn't going to like have legs and go on. Kind of the second thing though, a personal gripe of mine is that a lot of other meeting websites in order to attend an event, they force you to sign up and actually have an account with their site before you can attend that event. And so it was another big like design goal with Gathers Us was to make it a dead simple to both create an event and attend an event. Only information you need to provide is your first name, last name, and email. And then, you know, you can attend an event.

00:01:58.692 --> 00:02:01.396
<v Mike Hall>Do you ever have any problem with spam?

00:02:01.396 --> 00:02:09.230
<v Ethan Gunderson, Ryan Briones>I mean, because it's so easy to get in there. Yes. I mean, I know you have a CAPTCHA, but. That's the reason why.

00:02:09.230 --> 00:02:12.211
<v Mike Hall>Okay. And has that actually been effective?

00:02:12.211 --> 00:02:21.709
<v Ethan Gunderson, Ryan Briones>It hasn't happened since we introduced it. Oh, good. So. But, like you said, it was born out of a need when you were creating Chicago DB.

